  "body": "If _input_ to \"basic URL parser\" is the empty string, the algorithm is able to make it all the way through to the end, since there is no special check for empty string. That essentially means it returns a URL with all default values.\r\n\r\nIf that URL is then passed to \"URL serializer\", it returns `:` (just U+003A (:)).\r\n\r\nIs this all expected behavior? It seems to me like it wouldn't be.\r\n",
